  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5511",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with HuO-3N1 through multiple pathways, all of which involve the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is identified as a target of doxorubicin, and it is also a target of palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets HuO-3N1. The presence of multiple pathways linking doxorubicin to HuO-3N1 suggests a potential mechanism involving the inhibition of a purinoceptor, specifically P2X purinoceptor 1, which is a target of doxorubicin. The shared target of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate and palmarumycin CP18 further supports a common mode of action, possibly involving the modulation of purinoceptor signaling. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of a purinoceptor, which in turn affects the activity of HuO-3N1. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for doxorubicin to exert its effects through a specific molecular interaction that ultimately influences the function of HuO-3N1.",
